WEBVTT

00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:15,780
Beef was listed as a no one by protocol. Would that include grass-fed organic beef,

00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:24,660
and is elk, medicine, and buffalo okay to eat? Typically, when beef comes up as a no,

00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:34,100
it's no to grass-fed and organic as well, and it's a soft no to elk, medicine, and buffalo as well.

00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:42,820
Now again, this can change usually when I test a person and it does come up as meat as a driver,

00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:51,300
I do want to recheck that person within 30 days because just in my experience, it changes,

00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:58,420
but it doesn't always so. Some of you may be listening to me and you are off of meat and you've

00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:03,380
been off of meat for a year or two years or three years and you're doing real well. But

00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:09,460
most people that would meet come up a driver, I want to recheck again because most people,

00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:15,540
it changes quickly once we cut that out of your diet, clean up the gut, and then a person can go

00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:26,980
back on meat so we'll want to recheck that in 30 days.

